{
  "$schema": "https://aka.ms/codetour-schema",
  "title": "7: Aggregate sync (producer)",
  "description": "End-to-end: the opt-in, consent-gated path that rolls raw interactions into privacy-preserving aggregate buckets and POSTs them to the dashboard. This is the only code that sends anything off the machine. Every step embeds the numbered sequence diagram and points at the exact code for that step.",
  "nextTour": "8: Dashboard ingestion",
  "steps": [
    {
      "title": "Step 1 — Scheduled sync tick",
      "file": "src/extension/agent-observability-vscode/src/sync/scheduler.ts",
      "line": 29,
      "description": "![7: Aggregate sync (producer)](.tours/diagrams/d-46.svg)\n\n**▶ Step 1 of 8 in the sequence diagram — `SyncScheduler → SyncEngine: scheduled sync tick`**\n\n`SyncScheduler` fires a periodic tick (and one on activation) that drives the opt-in cloud sync. This is the ONLY path that sends anything off the machine."
    },
    {
      "title": "Step 2 — The consent gate",
      "file": "src/extension/agent-observability-vscode/src/sync/syncEngine.ts",
      "line": 195,
      "description": "![7: Aggregate sync (producer)](.tours/diagrams/d-47.svg)\n\n**▶ Step 2 of 8 in the sequence diagram — `SyncEngine → SyncEngine: computeCanSync() gate`**\n\n`computeCanSync` is the hard gate: sharing enabled, explicit consent recorded, and an API key present in SecretStorage. If any is missing, the run stops here — nothing is built or sent."
    },
    {
      "title": "Step 3 — Roll into aggregate buckets",
      "file": "src/extension/agent-observability-vscode/src/aggregate/aggregator.ts",
      "line": 124,
      "description": "![7: Aggregate sync (producer)](.tours/diagrams/d-48.svg)\n\n**▶ Step 3 of 8 in the sequence diagram — `SyncEngine → aggregator: buildBatch(rows)`**\n\n`buildBatch` rolls raw interactions into 30-minute buckets keyed by repo / model / developer — counts, duration sums, token sums, and a fixed-bound latency histogram. No prompt, completion, path, or identity text is included."
    },
    {
      "title": "Step 4 — Pseudonymous developer id",
      "file": "src/extension/agent-observability-vscode/src/aggregate/pseudonymizer.ts",
      "line": 49,
      "description": "![7: Aggregate sync (producer)](.tours/diagrams/d-49.svg)\n\n**▶ Step 4 of 8 in the sequence diagram — `SyncEngine → SyncEngine: computeDeveloperId (HMAC)`**\n\nThe only identity-derived value shipped is `computeDeveloperId` — an HMAC of a per-install salt and the identity input. It is irreversible and stable, so the dashboard can count developers without ever seeing one."
    },
    {
      "title": "Step 5 — Send the batch",
      "file": "src/extension/agent-observability-vscode/src/sync/syncClient.ts",
      "line": 94,
      "description": "![7: Aggregate sync (producer)](.tours/diagrams/d-50.svg)\n\n**▶ Step 5 of 8 in the sequence diagram — `SyncEngine → syncClient: sendBatch(batch)`**\n\n`SyncClient.sendBatch` serializes the batch and POSTs it with a Bearer key. The body is never logged or echoed; transport errors are scrubbed of the URL, headers, and key before surfacing."
    },
    {
      "title": "Step 6 — Hardcoded ingestion path",
      "file": "src/extension/agent-observability-vscode/src/sync/syncClient.ts",
      "line": 101,
      "description": "![7: Aggregate sync (producer)](.tours/diagrams/d-51.svg)\n\n**▶ Step 6 of 8 in the sequence diagram — `syncClient → Dashboard API: POST /api/ingest/aggregate`**\n\nThe target is `POST {dashboardUrl}/api/ingest/aggregate` — the path is a hardcoded constant, not a user setting, so the destination can't be silently redirected."
    },
    {
      "title": "Step 7 — Map the response",
      "file": "src/extension/agent-observability-vscode/src/sync/syncClient.ts",
      "line": 117,
      "description": "![7: Aggregate sync (producer)](.tours/diagrams/d-52.svg)\n\n**▶ Step 7 of 8 in the sequence diagram — `Dashboard API → syncClient: 200 accepted`**\n\n`mapStatus` turns the HTTP response into a typed outcome — 200 becomes success, 401/400 permanent failures, 429/5xx transient. The key is scrubbed from any human-readable detail."
    },
    {
      "title": "Step 8 — Advance or retry",
      "file": "src/extension/agent-observability-vscode/src/sync/syncEngine.ts",
      "line": 284,
      "description": "![7: Aggregate sync (producer)](.tours/diagrams/d-53.svg)\n\n**▶ Step 8 of 8 in the sequence diagram — `syncClient → SyncEngine: result`**\n\nBack in the engine, a success advances the watermark (and best-effort triggers flow 10); a permanent or retries-exhausted failure leaves the watermark unchanged so the same window retries next run — idempotent on the server."
    }
  ]
}
